%S A401777 1,6,36,291,1622,9015,47493,245422,1256244,6407698
%N A401777 Number of free polyhexes with 2n cells that can be dissected into two congruent polyhexes.
%C A401777 Here congruent means equal up to rotation, reflection and translation, so the two halves may be mirror images of each other. We call such a polyhex "halvable".
